// Orchicon RuntimeImage entity.
//
// A RuntimeImage is a tenant-owned buildable container image derived from
// the Orchicon runtime base image. Workers execute in one per-workflow-run
// runtime container; the image chosen for that container (via the bound
// work item's runtime_image) determines which tools/system libraries the
// worker has. Images are built by the runtime daemon (the only process with
// the Docker socket) from a structured spec — apt packages, toolchain
// install lines, and environment — plus an optional raw Dockerfile override.
// The base image is always part of the build: the daemon writes the
// `FROM <base>` line itself, and every built image inherits the
// `org.orchicon.runtime-base=true` label so the container-create gate
// accepts it.

